 CO 1228 PM MDT Mon Aug 24 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - This week will see daily afternoon thunderstorm chances, particularly along the higher terrain of western Colorado and eastern Utah. - Localized heavy rainfall continues to pose a threat to flash flooding over burn scars and susceptible terrain. - Daytime","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-08-24T18:35:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION... Moisture decreases this week, but enough remains in place to keep mountain showers and thunderstorms in the forecast each afternoon. The potential for localized heavy rainfall keeps flash flood and debris flow concerns elevated for newer burn scars and areas of susceptible terrain. Other concerns with afternoon convection include lightning and gusty outflow winds near or above 35 mp","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"hot02","station_name":"CSU Rogers Mesa Research Sta","distance_km":18.7,"soil_temp_5cm_f":87.33,"soil_temp_15cm_f":79.05,"soil_moisture_5cm":null,"soil_moisture_15cm":null,"precip_in":null,"eto_in":null,"vapor_pressure":null,"solar_radiation":286.67,"wind_speed_mph":5.89,"air_temp_f":85.32,"relative_humidity":0.266,"url":"https://coagmet.colostate.edu/station/hot02"},"aviation":{"icao":"KMTJ","distance_km":0,"raw_metar":"METAR KMTJ 242053Z AUTO 27007KT 10SM BKN120 29/07 A3027 RMK AO2 SLP169 T02940072 56021","temp_f":85,"wind_dir":270,"wind_kt":7,"gust_kt":null,"visibility":"10+","cover":"BKN","flight_category":"VFR","altimeter":1025.1,"observed":1787604780,"raw_taf":"TAF KMTJ 241720Z 2418/2518 36007KT P6SM FEW090 SCT250 PROB30 2418/2424 VRB15G30KT 4SM -TSRA BKN100CB FM250000 19005KT P6SM FEW110 SCT150 FM250300 14009KT P6SM FEW100 FEW250","url":"https://aviationweather.gov/data/metar/?ids=KMTJ&hours=0"},"airgradient":null,"airnow":{"aqi":47,"category":"Good","parameter":"O3","report